 {:db/id "q-110078/ma-source-field/c720090ff2c54eaac9f3df353427236068a8300cf6d0e6385f16d4903f1bbde6" :answer-field/id #uuid "fce68956-d8ec-5373-80c1-0576c6b35476" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-110078/ma-source-field/c720090ff2c54eaac9f3df353427236068a8300cf6d0e6385f16d4903f1bbde6/749ad78f6c2e244991175923f4accbcd688e83fd55c0c9780c94cf59d2b71e09" "q-110078/ma-source-field/c720090ff2c54eaac9f3df353427236068a8300cf6d0e6385f16d4903f1bbde6/783ec30e733ffa37545791abeec8239efe1dd0e1519e8b3ab461641365815f6e" "q-110078/ma-source-field/c720090ff2c54eaac9f3df353427236068a8300cf6d0e6385f16d4903f1bbde6/a5f20599553d766ff2ed6534424f99bf4cee2e744fd9922b2d06822c53843cc5" "q-110078/ma-source-field/c720090ff2c54eaac9f3df353427236068a8300cf6d0e6385f16d4903f1bbde6/746258203df4c9ed21ca911456f607018fd6cd12ae8e7b491b21a1103bfea187" "q-110078/ma-source-field/c720090ff2c54eaac9f3df353427236068a8300cf6d0e6385f16d4903f1bbde6/7b34feef3470ad2b12a577a625c1e7bebf3ed86e46c522c5cbf7bb5c78a06e29"] :answer-field/correct "q-110078/ma-source-field/c720090ff2c54eaac9f3df353427236068a8300cf6d0e6385f16d4903f1bbde6/a5f20599553d766ff2ed6534424f99bf4cee2e744fd9922b2d06822c53843cc5" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-110078" :question/id #uuid "b9a72356-7e05-5f10-b6ac-a2418c3b4fa6" :question/math-academy-id "q-110078" :question/problem "![](images/39/3905dacc3977857933a48ced329fc245b357f732aec520e67998efc0b5d7cdab.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" :question/worked-solution "Consider the line $x+2y=-8.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Writing the equation of this line in slope-intercept form, we have\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{2}x-4.\n$$\n\nNow, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\ge -\\frac{1}{2}x-4,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\nx+2y\\ge -8.\n$$\n\nNow consider the line $y=\\frac{1}{2}x+1.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\le \\frac{1}{2}x+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y\\ge -8 \\\\ y\\le \\frac{1}{2}x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-110078/ma-source-field/c720090ff2c54eaac9f3df353427236068a8300cf6d0e6385f16d4903f1bbde6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
