 {:db/id "q-112457/ma-source-field/5319a41e1dad76c3b1d3f97d8deb49bf6e68b9d7649d918b0d3b442438b45249" :answer-field/id #uuid "9feed68a-3a5e-5bf8-a32b-19c5c668ac59" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-112457/ma-source-field/5319a41e1dad76c3b1d3f97d8deb49bf6e68b9d7649d918b0d3b442438b45249/992e243681650f4ac292044aee6f4f8f8e8511c12a77ca20b89cbad3a675a903" "q-112457/ma-source-field/5319a41e1dad76c3b1d3f97d8deb49bf6e68b9d7649d918b0d3b442438b45249/5fdc2c6ae8bf1f63ffe96191b6d430c00f01dcbf5592c9cdd9ca44a95dfb639d" "q-112457/ma-source-field/5319a41e1dad76c3b1d3f97d8deb49bf6e68b9d7649d918b0d3b442438b45249/c6641a0f966e759926124877626ccb2cbfbb4ed82f69401067ecc7b9b70b7c4e" "q-112457/ma-source-field/5319a41e1dad76c3b1d3f97d8deb49bf6e68b9d7649d918b0d3b442438b45249/e6e38396a239b96245682f8c4870743f73d4b19ca4dac82e07060dc8bd27b66c" "q-112457/ma-source-field/5319a41e1dad76c3b1d3f97d8deb49bf6e68b9d7649d918b0d3b442438b45249/7a31257e19bafeea6c9a22fd9c98b8266dd2a204cd9ee3a371b1d98582a3f3d2"] :answer-field/correct "q-112457/ma-source-field/5319a41e1dad76c3b1d3f97d8deb49bf6e68b9d7649d918b0d3b442438b45249/e6e38396a239b96245682f8c4870743f73d4b19ca4dac82e07060dc8bd27b66c" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-112457" :question/id #uuid "fac39442-17f5-5ace-9954-931f61698611" :question/math-academy-id "q-112457" :question/problem "The equation ${t}^{2}-14t+5=5$ can be written in the form $(t+p{)}^{2}=q.$ Find $\\,pq\\,,$ and the sum of the roots ${t}_{1}+{t}_{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side and complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}-14t+5 & =5 \\\\ {t}^{2}-14t & =0 \\\\ {t}^{2}-2\\cdot t\\cdot 7+{7}^{2}-{7}^{2} & =0 \\\\ (t-7{)}^{2}-{7}^{2} & =0 \\\\ (t-7{)}^{2} & =49\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $p=-7$ and $q=49.$ Thus, $pq=-343.$\n\nWe now solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(t-7{)}^{2} & =49 \\\\ \\sqrt{(t-7{)}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{49} \\\\ |t-7| & =7 \\\\ t-7 & =\\pm 7 \\\\ t & =7\\pm 7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe simplify the two solutions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}_{1} & =7-7=0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & =7+7=14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum is ${t}_{1}+{t}_{2}=14.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-112457/ma-source-field/5319a41e1dad76c3b1d3f97d8deb49bf6e68b9d7649d918b0d3b442438b45249"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
