 {:db/id "q-112487/ma-source-field/d58b03810a050df5da1c7251d0346153429aca30cc557564f65af5c2c902976d" :answer-field/id #uuid "1d4fba57-c484-5fd0-a729-550a53e648f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-112487/ma-source-field/d58b03810a050df5da1c7251d0346153429aca30cc557564f65af5c2c902976d/4487146ec3ab1e0774cdd382ac7a45c0017a9088ac588299790df5a1dc3633ed" "q-112487/ma-source-field/d58b03810a050df5da1c7251d0346153429aca30cc557564f65af5c2c902976d/a34dc0647f6c5b916945eeb71389d121b25ce36151b448e86946b57af94a41ef" "q-112487/ma-source-field/d58b03810a050df5da1c7251d0346153429aca30cc557564f65af5c2c902976d/2f89b8665c948dc845a42f91d9e3de9e2b53473cedbb79acbe45970828e39794" "q-112487/ma-source-field/d58b03810a050df5da1c7251d0346153429aca30cc557564f65af5c2c902976d/e7246244c9d82c5699b691bf0636a1d30fe0c38416411d89130100da3fef8981" "q-112487/ma-source-field/d58b03810a050df5da1c7251d0346153429aca30cc557564f65af5c2c902976d/62c202b3a65b6b1213dfa29e02f710b8f3de6404410dbe0c32522080eba3fd3a"] :answer-field/correct "q-112487/ma-source-field/d58b03810a050df5da1c7251d0346153429aca30cc557564f65af5c2c902976d/2f89b8665c948dc845a42f91d9e3de9e2b53473cedbb79acbe45970828e39794" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-112487" :question/id #uuid "6d70e8a4-cad6-5c6f-b225-88fe32f8d423" :question/math-academy-id "q-112487" :question/problem "The equation ${m}^{2}+8=-8m$ can be written in the form $(m+p)^{2}=q.$ Find $p+q,$ and solve the equation." :question/worked-solution "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side, the $-8m$ term to the left-hand side, and complete the square on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{2}+8 & =-8m \\\\ {m}^{2}+8m & =-8 \\\\ {m}^{2}+2\\cdot 4\\cdot m & =-8 \\\\ {m}^{2}+2\\cdot 4\\cdot m+{4}^{2}-{4}^{2} & =-8 \\\\ (m+4)^{2}-{4}^{2} & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(m+4)^{2}-{4}^{2} & =-8 \\\\ (m+4)^{2} & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $p=4,q=8,$ and $p+q=12.$\n\nNext, we solve the equation using the square-root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(m+4)^{2} & =8 \\\\ \\sqrt{(m+4)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\ |m+4| & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\ m+4 & =\\pm 2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ m & =-4\\pm 2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-112487/ma-source-field/d58b03810a050df5da1c7251d0346153429aca30cc557564f65af5c2c902976d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
