 {:db/id "q-113245/ma-source-field/8f5478c32282a25c1be6f5b52a1feceae04751efec123b2722547303a13c5754" :answer-field/id #uuid "abb7896d-c7f4-5b7b-a55d-ac98d8904d0e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-113245/ma-source-field/8f5478c32282a25c1be6f5b52a1feceae04751efec123b2722547303a13c5754/e07c611192af075822ecf1844fc9b9bd50dbccd83259e0c40b56147e9677b780" "q-113245/ma-source-field/8f5478c32282a25c1be6f5b52a1feceae04751efec123b2722547303a13c5754/2b6b5b63fb8ecaea967cd7ac2863ce8bd58656d3ccc4ec1b14aec4077dcfb3c4" "q-113245/ma-source-field/8f5478c32282a25c1be6f5b52a1feceae04751efec123b2722547303a13c5754/5e9b625d4cdfd50931e6256d13df63e909e67d24a16ceb2dd816381e072bf2c8" "q-113245/ma-source-field/8f5478c32282a25c1be6f5b52a1feceae04751efec123b2722547303a13c5754/49053fd8b49cd1fcd9bb38fc30b5c5de3038bc0273d3aba53c51d3e8a5f8dfa3" "q-113245/ma-source-field/8f5478c32282a25c1be6f5b52a1feceae04751efec123b2722547303a13c5754/7c5b20195a3ec7b074300fa420393ddee4734e7e1fa089e2352f78a7188b789e"] :answer-field/correct "q-113245/ma-source-field/8f5478c32282a25c1be6f5b52a1feceae04751efec123b2722547303a13c5754/2b6b5b63fb8ecaea967cd7ac2863ce8bd58656d3ccc4ec1b14aec4077dcfb3c4" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-113245" :question/id #uuid "ed379096-4def-51e1-8cd6-e568b470e309" :question/math-academy-id "q-113245" :question/problem "The equation ${x}^{2}-6x+34=0$ can be written in the form $(x+p)^{2}=q.$ Find $p+q,$ and solve the equation." :question/worked-solution "We first move the constant to the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-6x+34 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-6x & =-34\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-6x & =-34 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2\\cdot 3x+{3}^{2}-{3}^{2} & =-34 \\\\ (x-3)^{2}-9 & =-34 \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =-25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=-3,\\,q=-25,$ and $p+q=-28.$\n\nFinally, we solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3)^{2} & =-25 \\\\ x-3 & =\\pm \\sqrt{-25} \\\\ x-3 & =\\pm 5\\,\\text{i} \\\\ x & =3\\pm 5\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has two solutions, $x=3+5\\,\\text{i}$ and $x=3-5\\,\\text{i}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-113245/ma-source-field/8f5478c32282a25c1be6f5b52a1feceae04751efec123b2722547303a13c5754"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
