 {:db/id "q-115265/ma-source-field/41e93c4662e01d1efaa8d3e164c56d8f6d74d294327ca631c5e7ad3c607ab861" :answer-field/id #uuid "6a10c896-987b-59f6-9202-743db84c67f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-115265/ma-source-field/41e93c4662e01d1efaa8d3e164c56d8f6d74d294327ca631c5e7ad3c607ab861/d789f516e75cdba3a7ae0a072cfbd5d7ee75d431526b449647b8bd0d516d464b" "q-115265/ma-source-field/41e93c4662e01d1efaa8d3e164c56d8f6d74d294327ca631c5e7ad3c607ab861/39cc36d9f2c2507795fd5d3b7f1e6e191ce6cbea7853e63ba81016d9d99d080d" "q-115265/ma-source-field/41e93c4662e01d1efaa8d3e164c56d8f6d74d294327ca631c5e7ad3c607ab861/8962ea8d31664ff72197b61583aaa938ae2b85d21604fb9ad6adf9b2cb4960be" "q-115265/ma-source-field/41e93c4662e01d1efaa8d3e164c56d8f6d74d294327ca631c5e7ad3c607ab861/f78ba7a19cd6344c2d1c418ca5fb70790ae0c77010ee7afb3df9db320d262386" "q-115265/ma-source-field/41e93c4662e01d1efaa8d3e164c56d8f6d74d294327ca631c5e7ad3c607ab861/f1613f4d908ea656ed8f8bde3574b0b60d04ae5ef7a93dc43d04d854b08b6348"] :answer-field/correct "q-115265/ma-source-field/41e93c4662e01d1efaa8d3e164c56d8f6d74d294327ca631c5e7ad3c607ab861/8962ea8d31664ff72197b61583aaa938ae2b85d21604fb9ad6adf9b2cb4960be" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-115265" :question/id #uuid "f5a82529-6969-5fb0-8f80-d44b22e50fb0" :question/math-academy-id "q-115265" :question/problem "The graph of the function $y=f(x)$ passes through $(1,2)$ and is concave up on the interval $(0,2).$ If ${f}^{′}(1)=-2,$ estimate the value of $f(0.8)$ using the tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at $x=1$ and determine whether the approximation is an underestimate or overestimate." :question/worked-solution "The tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at the point $a=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a) \\\\  & =f(1)+{f}^{′}(1)(x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function passes through the point $(1,2),$ so we have $f(1)=2.$ Also, we're told that ${f}^{′}(1)=-2,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =2+(-2)(x-1) \\\\  & =2-2(x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $f(0.8)$ by evaluating the tangent line approximation at $x=0.8.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.8) & ≈L(0.8) \\\\  & =2-2(0.8-1) \\\\  & =2-2(-0.2) \\\\  & =2.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the function is concave up on the interval $(0,2),$ the linear approximation $L(x)$ is below the graph close to $x=1,$ and therefore we have an underestimate." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-115265/ma-source-field/41e93c4662e01d1efaa8d3e164c56d8f6d74d294327ca631c5e7ad3c607ab861"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
