 {:db/id "q-115364/ma-source-field/839e883381ece995ad6b8a075946d3d45b780d3f429634ce2aca2e4930e4b313" :answer-field/id #uuid "6a898ac5-9ac8-57ea-9a3a-e0a38e6b53ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-115364/ma-source-field/839e883381ece995ad6b8a075946d3d45b780d3f429634ce2aca2e4930e4b313/820974c59806794e83f28d53072c0693c6465b277b2b2d3ff2185a3b40ccb4c3" "q-115364/ma-source-field/839e883381ece995ad6b8a075946d3d45b780d3f429634ce2aca2e4930e4b313/18916eef2b50adb127ef32f85f7a0f61094cb9d534a34fe1b392b9cfb663b7fa" "q-115364/ma-source-field/839e883381ece995ad6b8a075946d3d45b780d3f429634ce2aca2e4930e4b313/9e321fb8df7b3d7b5a2e6e77a54b3c03c8242f48fd5f9843c5ac6549d81be25e" "q-115364/ma-source-field/839e883381ece995ad6b8a075946d3d45b780d3f429634ce2aca2e4930e4b313/1f09d62c1ef167549e34c25039ee473a37b01627ac55dcc57f3fe2e4a2d494bb" "q-115364/ma-source-field/839e883381ece995ad6b8a075946d3d45b780d3f429634ce2aca2e4930e4b313/6e8b450743f4547cc7e473fe8cb1077849a55d58e2d87ba449f5c4130f1f6572"] :answer-field/correct "q-115364/ma-source-field/839e883381ece995ad6b8a075946d3d45b780d3f429634ce2aca2e4930e4b313/9e321fb8df7b3d7b5a2e6e77a54b3c03c8242f48fd5f9843c5ac6549d81be25e" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-115364" :question/id #uuid "a02e3599-0d24-591c-985f-c45e9f652ee9" :question/math-academy-id "q-115364" :question/problem "![](images/3a/3af3101fd7a103e8382755177ca1ebab9bc1cdf48aebd34af8ac7cc92991387c.png)\n\nGiven that the points $(-1,2)$ and $(1,4)$ lie on a diameter of a circle, what are the center and radius of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The center of the circle is located at the midpoint of the diameter. So, we can calculate the coordinates of the center using the midpoint formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(h,k) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{-1+1}{2},\\frac{2+4}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{0}{2},\\frac{6}{2}) \\\\  & =(0,3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe radius can be found by calculating the distance between the center $(0,3)$ and a point on the circle, such as $(-1,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\sqrt{{({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})}^{2}+{({y}_{1}-{y}_{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(-1-0)}^{2}+{(2-3)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-115364/ma-source-field/839e883381ece995ad6b8a075946d3d45b780d3f429634ce2aca2e4930e4b313"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
